  "description": "Two seams over an amateur-radio transceiver, both dependency-free and capability-probed: IRigControl, the station-control (CAT) seam for frequency, mode, PTT and SWR/RF-power metering; and IRadioControl, the channel-sensing seam for RSSI, hardware carrier-sense (DCD) edges and transmitter keying, plus IRadioSideChannel for radio-native small-datagram messaging. RigRadioControl bridges any IRigControl to IRadioControl by polling its receive-side reads. Implementations: M0LTE.Rig.Hamlib and M0LTE.Rig.Flrig for IRigControl; M0LTE.Tait.Ccdi implements both seams natively for Tait TM8100/TM8200 radios. Source: github.com/M0LTE/M0LTE.Rig.",
